<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>救生艇新闻：博客——保护人类</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/</link><description></description><lastBuildDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 12:25:01 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>长程磁相互作用控制亚铁磁体如何实现相变</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/long-range-magnetic-interactions-govern-how-a-ferrimagnet-approaches-its-phase-transition</link><description>接近相变时，非常不同的材料可以遵循相同的数学规则。普遍性的概念是为了描述这种现象而提出的，该概念根据看似不同的系统的共同属性对其进行分组。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/long-range-magnetic-interactions-govern-how-a-ferrimagnet-approaches-its-phase-transition2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 12:24:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/long-range-magnetic-interactions-govern-how-a-ferrimagnet-approaches-its-phase-transition</guid></item><item><title>氪气成为量子计算的新成分</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/krypton-gas-emerges-as-a-new-ingredient-for-quantum-computing</link><description>为了实现量子计算的商业化，制造商需要用于微芯片的高质量超导材料，但他们也需要可靠、可持续的纳米制造工艺。钽是一种耐腐蚀金属，满足第一个标准，但不满足第二个标准。这是因为它必须在通常超过 400°C (752°F) 的温度下沉积在基板上，这对于许多半导体铸造厂当前的工具来说太热了。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/krypton-gas-emerges-as-a-new-ingredient-for-quantum-computing.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 12:09:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/krypton-gas-emerges-as-a-new-ingredient-for-quantum-computing</guid></item><item><title>迄今为止最大的人类细胞如何读取 DNA 的目录显示了化学标记如何改变遗传指令</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/largest-catalog-yet-of-how-human-cells-read-dna-shows-how-chemical-marks-alter-genetic-instructions</link><description>体内的每个细胞基本上都含有相同的 DNA，但脑细胞的行为与肌肉细胞或免疫细胞不同。差异主要在于每个细胞如何读取其遗传指令。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/largest-catalog-yet-of-how-human-cells-read-dna-shows-how-chemical-marks-alter-genetic-instructions.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 11:54:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/largest-catalog-yet-of-how-human-cells-read-dna-shows-how-chemical-marks-alter-genetic-instructions</guid></item><item><title>谷不平衡菱面体石墨烯可能出现不寻常的超导性</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/unusual-superconductivity-could-emerge-in-valley-imbalanced-rhombohedral-graphene</link><description>超导体是电流以零电阻流动的材料，通常低于特定温度。在传统的超导体中，当两个电子在低温下结合在一起形成所谓的库珀对时，就会出现这种物质状态。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/unusual-superconductivity-could-emerge-in-valley-imbalanced-rhombohedral-graphene2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 11:39:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/unusual-superconductivity-could-emerge-in-valley-imbalanced-rhombohedral-graphene</guid></item><item><title>构建抗噪声量子传感器的新方法</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/a-new-approach-to-building-noise-resistant-quantum-sensors</link><description>量子传感器是一种利用量子力学现象收集测量值的设备，可以比传统传感器具有更高的灵敏度来检测极弱的磁、引力和电磁信号。一些量子传感器利用纠缠，这种现象促使遥远的粒子变得如此紧密地联系在一起，以至于一个粒子的物理状态决定了其他粒子的状态。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/a-new-approach-to-building-noise-resistant-quantum-sensors2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 11:24:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/a-new-approach-to-building-noise-resistant-quantum-sensors</guid></item><item><title>新的光子晶体方法改进了量子网络的单光子源</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/new-photonic-crystal-method-improves-single-photon-sources-for-quantum-networks</link><description>与当今的标准技术相比，量子通信具有许多优势，包括绝对安全地传输大量数据。然而，它需要单光子，并且产生它们非常困难。慕尼黑工业大学 (TUM) 和慕尼黑量子科学技术中心 (MCQST) 的研究人员开发了一种新方法，克服了以前方法的问题。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/new-photonic-crystal-method-improves-single-photon-sources-for-quantum-networks.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 11:09:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/new-photonic-crystal-method-improves-single-photon-sources-for-quantum-networks</guid></item><item><title>科学家“看到”纳米级力，提供了空气-水界面存在电场的证据</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/scientists-see-nanoscale-forces-providing-evidence-of-electric-fields-at-the-air-water-interface</link><description>气泡是圆形的，我们知道表面张力就是圆形的。但是，将气液边界压缩到只有几十纳米宽的空间中——是否还有其他力在起作用？ &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/scientists-see-nanoscale-forces-providing-evidence-of-electric-fields-at-the-air-water-interface.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 10:54:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/scientists-see-nanoscale-forces-providing-evidence-of-electric-fields-at-the-air-water-interface</guid></item><item><title>曲面重塑活性材料，将缺陷附近的振动局部化</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/curved-surfaces-reshape-active-materials-localizing-vibrations-near-defects</link><description>许多材料，无论是生物材料还是工程材料，都是由内部提供动力的。科学家们已经彻底研究了这种“活性”材料的运作方式，但到目前为止，大多是在环境曲率不起作用的情况下进行的。研究中&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/curved-surfaces-reshape-active-materials-localizing-vibrations-near-defects2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 10:39:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/curved-surfaces-reshape-active-materials-localizing-vibrations-near-defects</guid></item><item><title>激光稳定性方法提高了光电子的精确控制</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/laser-stability-method-advances-precision-control-of-electrons-with-light</link><description>奥尔登堡大学物理研究所的研究人员正在研究精确控制光电场的技术，该技术允许在实验中操纵单个电子的动力学。现在，Jan Vogelsang 博士领导的阿秒显微镜研究小组已朝着这一目标迈出了决定性的一步。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/laser-stability-method-advances-precision-control-of-electrons-with-light.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 10:24:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/laser-stability-method-advances-precision-control-of-electrons-with-light</guid></item><item><title>基于声音的陷阱揭示了脆弱的生物分子液滴如何移动、合并和改变硬度</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/sound-based-traps-reveal-how-fragile-biomolecular-droplets-move-merge-and-change-stiffness</link><description>&lt;img src="https://politepaul.com/fd/dtDF30237DhP.xml" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 10:09:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/sound-based-traps-reveal-how-fragile-biomolecular-droplets-move-merge-and-change-stiffness</guid></item></channel></rss>